o a flat ticket dir.","src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py:115 `def _unlink_would_cancel(tracker: str, source: str, target: str)` reads the ordered-pair link on the source ticket's dir."],"finding":"Step 4's 'Required inventory' of flat ticket-path consumers to route through the layout helper omits `rebar._commands.doctor`, which constructs a ticket dir at `Path(tracker) / source` (a ticket id) inside `_unlink_would_cancel` and passes it to `_get_link_info`. A grep sweep for `Path(tracker) /` shows this site; it is absent from the command list (which does enumerate transition, txn, unlink, link_revert, etc.).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffcc7a53264434b75","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan step 4, 'Required inventory: ... commands {…}'","norm_id":"nbc45b1467b65a283","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["After a store is migrated to shards, `doctor`'s `_unlink_would_cancel`/`classify_edge` path resolves `Path(tracker) / source` to a non-existent flat dir, so `_get_link_info` sees no events and doctor misclassifies or crashes on every link check — an unpatched call site the inventory misses."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Route doctor.py's `Path(tracker) / source` through the layout helper's existing-dir resolution and confirm no other `Path(tracker) / <id>` sites (e.g. verify the reconciler/graph sweep) are unlisted.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how an empty shard container (post-rollback, or pre-populated) is classified by the depth-aware fsck `foreign_store_path_list`/`_holds_events` and whether writers or the migration ever leave/clean empty shard dirs, so an empty shard is neither reported FOREIGN nor swept.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["staging.py StagedEvent.unpublish (L201-215) only os.rmdir(self.ticket_dir); it does not remove the parent shard container it may have just created via the step-2 exist_ok mkdir","fsck_tracker_health.foreign_store_path_list._holds_events (L122-138) treats any top-level non-dot dir holding no event file as foreign; step 7 makes it depth-aware for 'valid shard containers' but does not define an EMPTY shard container's classification","Step 2: 'an empty shard container remains benign' — asserted but the fsck classifier contract for the empty case is not stated in step 7"],"finding":"The plan does not specify how an empty shard container (left behind when StagedEvent.unpublish rolls back a create by removing only the ticket_dir, not its now-empty parent shard) is classified by the depth-aware fsck/store-health check, risking a benign empty shard being reported as FOREIGN_STORE_PATH or, worse, swept by tracker-maintenance.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3d5613496cefeb0d","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan steps 2 and 7; AC 'leaves no flat ticket dirs behind'","norm_id":"n460dde9d25994a64","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A create transaction rolls back (validation failure / OCC abort) after the shard mkdir but the ticket dir is removed, leaving tickets/<shard>/ empty","fsck runs and either mislabels the empty shard FOREIGN_STORE_PATH or tracker-maintenance sweeps it"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State in step 7 that a directory whose name matches the shard-container shape (recognized by the layout helper) is store data regardless of whether it currently contains ticket subdirs, and confirm in step 2 whether unpublish leaves the empty shard (documented benign) or removes it under the lock.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["86 file-impact entries (> 30)"],"finding":"Oversize signals suggest this unit may be too large for one session.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb59727dfac76fbbf","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"nd8e22e5830cb74a7","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"If this really is more than one unit of work, split it into coherent child tickets (G5 decomposition) so each is one session's work. If instead the plan is merely long-winded, tighten the prose and move narration into ticket comments or a session log rather than fragmenting coherent work. Run `rebar explain plan` for the authoring guidance.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the exact sha256 prefix width (e.g. first 2 hex chars = 256 shards) used to derive the shard container, so fan-out is deterministic and the 80%-reduction AC is achievable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.332,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'fan-out layout tickets/<sha256-id-prefix>/<id>'","AC: 'top-level tree bytes at least 80% smaller than an equivalent flat layout'","step 1: 'sha256-based shard/relpath derivation' — width not stated"],"finding":"The shard key 'sha256-id-prefix' never specifies how many characters/bytes of the sha256 hex prefix form the shard container, yet this fan-out width directly determines the top-level tree size and thus whether the 80%-reduction AC can be met.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe3d217a6c05715f6","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / AC line 1 / Implementation Plan step 1","norm_id":"n3ce537211240effb","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor picks a 1-char prefix (16 buckets) vs 2-char (256 buckets); with ~6008 tickets these give very different per-commit root-tree sizes and reduction ratios."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify the prefix length in Scope and step 1, e.g. 'shard = first 2 hex chars of sha256(canonical-id), giving 256 containers'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the sha256 shard-prefix length and expected entries-per-shard for ~6,008 tickets, justified against established fan-out practice (e.g., git .git/objects 2-char prefix, CocoaPods hash-sharding), so the 80% tree-shrink AC is reproducible.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.432,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'sha256-based shard/relpath derivation' with no stated prefix length or fan-out ratio","Prior art (retrieved): github.blog 'Git's database internals V' and nesbitt.io (Dec 2025) describe CocoaPods fixing 16,000 flat directories via 'hash-based sharding: split directories by the first few characters of a hashed name'; git .git/objects uses a 2-char sha prefix","ABSENCE: with ~6,008 tickets, whether the 80% tree-shrink AC holds depends entirely on the unstated prefix width (e.g., 1 vs 2 hex chars -> 16 vs 256 shards)"],"finding":"The plan adopts sha256 prefix fan-out (an established pattern used by git's own .git/objects and by CocoaPods' hash-sharding of large flat Specs dirs) but never states the shard-prefix length or the expected entries-per-shard for 6,008 tickets, leaving the load-bearing design parameter borrowed from that prior art unpinned.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f01ece3a30dc299bf","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan step 1; AC line 'top-level tree bytes at least 80% smaller'","norm_id":"nb523a15bf42fbad2","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A prefix too short leaves shards still large enough to miss the 80% tree-shrink target","A prefix too long creates thousands of near-empty shard dirs, adding its own root-tree churn"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_